-- LAYER 1: section 2025(h)(1)(F), pilot projects to reduce dependency and increase work requirements and work effort
-- (7 U.S.C. 2025; lines 2154-2278 of usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / JUST n is what the text says, NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md, Reading a result).
-- "Good cause" and "work registrant" are not defined in this subparagraph (NOTES.md, finding 1); a caller who has an answer supplies it as an input.

§ `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(i) Pilot projects required`

-- src:2157 | The Secretary shall carry out pilot projects under which State agencies shall enter into cooperative agreements with the Secretary to develop and test methods, including operating work programs with certain features comparable to the program of block grants to States for temporary assistance for needy families established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), for employment and training programs and services to raise the number of work registrants under section 2015(d) of this title who obtain unsubsidized employment, increase the earned income of the registrants, and reduce the reliance of the registrants on public assistance, so as to reduce the need for supplemental nutrition assistance benefits.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(i)(I) the Secretary shall carry out pilot projects (src:2157)
GIVEN `the Secretary carries out pilot projects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `State agencies enter into cooperative agreements with the Secretary to develop and test methods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(i)(I) the Secretary has carried out the pilot projects as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary carries out pilot projects` AND `State agencies enter into cooperative agreements with the Secretary to develop and test methods` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall carry out pilot projects under which State agencies shall enter into cooperative agreements with the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2159 | Pilot projects shall—
-- src:2160 | (aa) meet such terms and conditions as the Secretary considers to be appropriate; and
-- src:2161 | (bb) except as otherwise provided in this subparagraph, be in accordance with the requirements of sections 2015(d) and 2029 of this title.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(i)(II) requirements of the pilot projects (src:2159-2161)
GIVEN `the pilot project meets the terms and conditions the Secretary considers to be appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pilot project is in accordance with the requirements of sections 2015(d) and 2029` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this subparagraph provides otherwise for the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(i)(II) the pilot project meets the requirements` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the pilot project meets the terms and conditions the Secretary considers to be appropriate` AND (`the pilot project is in accordance with the requirements of sections 2015(d) and 2029` OR `this subparagraph provides otherwise for the requirement`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Pilot projects shall— (aa) meet such terms and conditions as the Secretary considers to be appropriate"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii) Selection criteria`

-- src:2164 | The Secretary shall select pilot projects under this subparagraph in accordance with the criteria established under this clause and additional criteria established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(I) select pilot projects in accordance with the criteria (src:2164)
GIVEN `the Secretary selects the pilot project in accordance with the criteria established under this clause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary selects the pilot project in accordance with the additional criteria the Secretary has established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(I) the Secretary has selected the pilot project as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary selects the pilot project in accordance with the criteria established under this clause` AND `the Secretary selects the pilot project in accordance with the additional criteria the Secretary has established` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall select pilot projects under this subparagraph in accordance with the criteria established under this clause and additional criteria established by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2166 | To be eligible to participate in a pilot project, a State agency shall—
-- src:2167 | (aa) agree to participate in the evaluation described in clause (vii), including providing evidence that the State has a robust data collection system for program administration and cooperating to make available State data on the employment activities and post-participation employment, earnings, and public benefit receipt of participants to ensure proper and timely evaluation;
-- src:2168 | (bb) commit to collaborate with the State workforce board and other job training programs in the State and local area; and
-- src:2169 | (cc) commit to maintain at least the amount of State funding for employment and training programs and services under paragraphs (2) and (3) and under section 2029 of this title as the State expended for fiscal year 2013.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(II) qualifying criteria for a State agency (src:2166-2169)
GIVEN `the State agency agrees to participate in the evaluation described in clause (vii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency provides evidence that the State has a robust data collection system for program administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency cooperates to make available State data on the employment activities and post-participation employment, earnings, and public benefit receipt of participants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency commits to collaborate with the State workforce board and other job training programs in the State and local area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency commits to maintain at least the amount of State funding for employment and training programs and services as the State expended for fiscal year 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(II) the State agency meets the qualifying criteria` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency agrees to participate in the evaluation described in clause (vii)`
            AND `the State agency provides evidence that the State has a robust data collection system for program administration`
            AND `the State agency cooperates to make available State data on the employment activities and post-participation employment, earnings, and public benefit receipt of participants`
            AND `the State agency commits to collaborate with the State workforce board and other job training programs in the State and local area`
            AND `the State agency commits to maintain at least the amount of State funding for employment and training programs and services as the State expended for fiscal year 2013`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To be eligible to participate in a pilot project, a State agency shall"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2169 | (cc) commit to maintain at least the amount of State funding for employment and training programs and services under paragraphs (2) and (3) and under section 2029 of this title as the State expended for fiscal year 2013.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(II)(cc) maintain at least the fiscal year 2013 amount (src:2169)
GIVEN `State funding the State agency commits to maintain, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `State funding the State expended for fiscal year 2013, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(II)(cc) the commitment is at least the amount expended for fiscal year 2013` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `State funding the State agency commits to maintain, in dollars` AT LEAST `State funding the State expended for fiscal year 2013, in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "commit to maintain at least the amount of State funding"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2171 | In selecting pilot projects, the Secretary shall—
-- src:2172 | (aa) consider the degree to which the pilot project would enhance existing employment and training programs in the State;
-- src:2173 | (bb) consider the degree to which the pilot project would enhance the employment and earnings of program participants;
-- src:2174 | (cc) consider whether there is evidence that the pilot project could be replicated easily by other States or political subdivisions;
-- src:2175 | (dd) consider whether the State agency has a demonstrated capacity to operate high quality employment and training programs; and
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(III)(aa)-(dd) the Secretary considers (src:2171-2175)
GIVEN `the Secretary considers the degree to which the pilot project would enhance existing employment and training programs in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary considers the degree to which the pilot project would enhance the employment and earnings of program participants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary considers whether there is evidence that the pilot project could be replicated easily by other States or political subdivisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary considers whether the State agency has a demonstrated capacity to operate high quality employment and training programs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(III) the Secretary has considered the factors in selecting the pilot project` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary considers the degree to which the pilot project would enhance existing employment and training programs in the State`
            AND `the Secretary considers the degree to which the pilot project would enhance the employment and earnings of program participants`
            AND `the Secretary considers whether there is evidence that the pilot project could be replicated easily by other States or political subdivisions`
            AND `the Secretary considers whether the State agency has a demonstrated capacity to operate high quality employment and training programs`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In selecting pilot projects, the Secretary shall— (aa) consider the degree to which the pilot project would enhance existing employment and training programs in the State"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2176 | (ee) ensure the pilot projects, when considered as a group, test a range of strategies, including strategies that—
-- src:2177 | (AA) target individuals with low skills or limited work experience, individuals subject to the requirements under section 2015(o) of this title, and individuals who are working;
-- src:2178 | (BB) are located in a range of geographic areas and States, including rural and urban areas;
-- src:2179 | (CC) emphasize education and training, rehabilitative services for individuals with barriers to employment, rapid attachment to employment, and mixed strategies; and
-- src:2180 | (DD) test programs that assign work registrants to mandatory and voluntary participation in employment and training activities.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(III)(ee) the pilot projects considered as a group (src:2176-2180)
GIVEN `the pilot projects, when considered as a group, test a range of strategies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include strategies that target individuals with low skills or limited work experience, individuals subject to the requirements under section 2015(o), and individuals who are working` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include strategies that are located in a range of geographic areas and States, including rural and urban areas` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include strategies that emphasize education and training, rehabilitative services for individuals with barriers to employment, rapid attachment to employment, and mixed strategies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include strategies that test programs that assign work registrants to mandatory and voluntary participation in employment and training activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ii)(III)(ee) the Secretary has ensured that the group of pilot projects tests the strategies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the pilot projects, when considered as a group, test a range of strategies`
            AND `they include strategies that target individuals with low skills or limited work experience, individuals subject to the requirements under section 2015(o), and individuals who are working`
            AND `they include strategies that are located in a range of geographic areas and States, including rural and urban areas`
            AND `they include strategies that emphasize education and training, rehabilitative services for individuals with barriers to employment, rapid attachment to employment, and mixed strategies`
            AND `they include strategies that test programs that assign work registrants to mandatory and voluntary participation in employment and training activities`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ensure the pilot projects, when considered as a group, test a range of strategies, including strategies that"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iii) Accountability`

-- src:2183 | The Secretary shall establish and implement a process to terminate a pilot project for which the State has failed to meet the criteria described in clause (ii) or other criteria established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iii)(I) the process to terminate a pilot project (src:2183)
GIVEN `the Secretary has established a process to terminate a pilot project for which the State has failed to meet the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has implemented the process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iii)(I) the Secretary has established and implemented the termination process` MEANS
    BRANCH
