        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall establish and implement a process to terminate a pilot project"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2185 | The process shall include a reasonable time period, not to exceed 180 days, for State agencies found noncompliant to correct the noncompliance.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iii)(II) a reasonable time period, not to exceed 180 days (src:2185)
GIVEN `the time period is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days allowed for State agencies found noncompliant to correct the noncompliance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iii)(II) the time period allowed to correct the noncompliance is as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the time period is reasonable` AND `days allowed for State agencies found noncompliant to correct the noncompliance` AT MOST 180 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The process shall include a reasonable time period, not to exceed 180 days"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iv) Employment and training activities`

-- src:2187 | Allowable programs and services carried out under this subparagraph shall include those programs and services authorized under this chapter and employment and training activities authorized under the program of block grants to States for temporary assistance for needy families established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.), including:
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iv) allowable programs and services (src:2187)
GIVEN `the program or service is authorized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is an employment and training activity authorized under the program of block grants to States for temporary assistance for needy families established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is one of those described in subclauses (I) to (XII)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(iv) the program or service is allowable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the program or service is authorized under this chapter` OR `the activity is an employment and training activity authorized under the program of block grants to States for temporary assistance for needy families established under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` OR `the activity is one of those described in subclauses (I) to (XII)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Allowable programs and services carried out under this subparagraph shall include those programs and services authorized under this chapter and employment and training activities authorized under the program of block grants"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

