§ `s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix) Use of funds`

-- src:2270 | Funds made available under this subparagraph for pilot projects shall be used only for—
-- src:2271 | (aa) pilot projects that comply with this chapter;
-- src:2272 | (bb) the program and administrative costs of carrying out the pilot projects;
-- src:2273 | (cc) the costs incurred in developing systems and providing information and data for the independent evaluations under clause (vii); and
-- src:2274 | (dd) the costs of the evaluations under clause (vii).
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(I) used only for (src:2270-2274)
GIVEN `the use is for pilot projects that comply with this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the program and administrative costs of carrying out the pilot projects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the costs incurred in developing systems and providing information and data for the independent evaluations under clause (vii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for the costs of the evaluations under clause (vii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(I) the funds may be used for the use` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the use is for pilot projects that comply with this chapter` OR `the use is for the program and administrative costs of carrying out the pilot projects` OR `the use is for the costs incurred in developing systems and providing information and data for the independent evaluations under clause (vii)` OR `the use is for the costs of the evaluations under clause (vii)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Funds made available under this subparagraph for pilot projects shall be used only for"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2276 | Funds made available under this subparagraph shall be used only to supplement, not to supplant, non-Federal funds used for existing employment and training activities or services.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(II) supplement, not supplant (src:2276)
GIVEN `the funds are used to supplement non-Federal funds used for existing employment and training activities or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the funds are used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing employment and training activities or services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(II) the funds are used as the text allows` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the funds are used to supplement non-Federal funds used for existing employment and training activities or services` AND (NOT `the funds are used to supplant non-Federal funds used for existing employment and training activities or services`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be used only to supplement, not to supplant, non-Federal funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2278 | In carrying out pilot projects, States may contribute additional funds obtained from other sources, including Federal, State, or private funds, on the condition that the use of the contributions is permissible under Federal law.
@ref s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(III) States may contribute additional funds (src:2278)
GIVEN `the funds are obtained from other sources, including Federal, State, or private funds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use of the contributions is permissible under Federal law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2025(h)(1)(F)(ix)(III) the State may contribute the additional funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the condition that the use of the contributions is permissible under Federal law"
        IF (NOT `the use of the contributions is permissible under Federal law`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the funds are obtained from other sources, including Federal, State, or private funds` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "States may contribute additional funds obtained from other sources"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
